// CHARACTERIZATION — current behaviour is incorrect, fixed in PR3.
//
// `email` is a new required column (no `@default`) added to a table that
// already exists in `prev`. `diffTable`'s added-column loop emits a plain,
// UNGUARDED `ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN "email" text NOT NULL;` — which
// fails outright against any table already holding rows ("column contains
// null values"). PR3 refuses generation with a
// `required-column-without-default` diagnostic instead of emitting DDL
// that is guaranteed to fail on populated tables.

Table User {
  id    Int    @id @default(autoincrement())
  email String
}
